From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 03:24:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Report the target interpreter in debug and the user agent

pip's debug page and user agent describe the Python pip runs in, which
is the one it installs for. Compiled, kpip runs in a CPython of its own:
debug printed that bundle's version and implementation, and a
sys.executable that does not exist, beside tags for the target, and the
user agent credited every install to the bundled CPython. The user agent
now reports the target's version and implementation, from its markers.
debug shows the target python (executable, version, implementation,
platform), saying when none was found, and kpip's own runtime on a line
of its own.
